BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Lives of Others (35mm) (2006)
DTSTART:20260723T020000Z
DTEND:20260723T043500Z
DTSTAMP:20260723T020000Z
UID:NNAKEpQ6dJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 137 mins (2h17m)\n\nIn 1983 East Berlin\, a dedicate
 d Stasi officer\, doubting that a famous playwright and his actress-lover 
 are loyal to the Communist Party\, receives approval to spy on them\, beco
 ming unexpectedly sympathetic to the couple until he is ordered to take it
  a step farther.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/cold-war-summ
 er/the-lives-of-others\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Manchurian Candidate (1962)
DTSTART:20260730T020000Z
DTEND:20260730T042500Z
DTSTAMP:20260730T020000Z
UID:5KBorHSSTy
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 126 mins (2h06m)\n\nSet in the early fifties\, this 
 razor-sharp adaptation of the novel by Richard Condon concerns a decorated
  U.S. Army sergeant\, who as a prisoner during the Korean War is brainwash
 ed into becoming a sleeper assassin in a Communist conspiracy\, and a fell
 ow POW who slowly uncovers the sinister plot.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/prog
 rams-and-events/cold-war-summer/the-manchurian-candidate\n\nEstimated star
 t: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Once Upon a Time in a Cinema
DTSTART:20260730T230000Z
DTEND:20260731T011000Z
DTSTAMP:20260730T230000Z
UID:8tBwyrIEXN
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nBurst pipes\, rats and financial
  pressure torment a Limerick theatre owner in 1984 in David Gleeson's hear
 twarming love letter to cinemas.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-even
 ts/art-house-theater-day-2026/once-upon-a-time-in-a-cinema\n\nEstimated st
 art: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sorry to Bother You (2018)
DTSTART:20260731T020000Z
DTEND:20260731T041000Z
DTSTAMP:20260731T020000Z
UID:Q331Q5w5Kq
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 112 mins (1h52m)\n\nLakeith Stanfield\, Tessa Thomps
 on\, and Steven Yuen star in the exhilarating directorial debut of musicia
 n Boots Riley\, a biting and bonkers satire that follows a black telemarke
 ter who discovers an unknown skill which gives him magical selling powers 
 that shoot him up the corporate ladder.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-
 theaters/sorry-to-bother-you\n\nEstimated start: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Network (1976)
DTSTART:20260801T230000Z
DTEND:20260802T012000Z
DTSTAMP:20260801T230000Z
UID:qPcxpRcy4H
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 121 mins (2h01m)\n\nThis media satire\, directed by 
 Sidney Lumet from a brilliantly incisive script by Paddy Chayefsky\, is an
  X-ray of the corrupted soul of a corporate-dominated America\, startlingl
 y prescient in its anticipation of today’s outrage-driven news cycle. 50
 th anniversary screening.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/art-
 house-theater-day-2026/network\n\nEstimated start: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Car Wash (1976)
DTSTART:20260802T230000Z
DTEND:20260803T005500Z
DTSTAMP:20260802T230000Z
UID:3Bk4ht5sqS
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 97 mins (1h37m)\n\nAt Sully Boyar's car wash\, every
 body is cleaning up and getting down in this classic comedy with a killer 
 soundtrack. 50th anniversary screening.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-a
